<title>UK: UK Labour - utilities will face windfall tax.</title>
<headline>UK Labour - utilities will face windfall tax.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A British Labour government would impose a windfall tax on privatised utilities to raise funds to help tackle unemployment, shadow finance minister for Britain's opposition Labour Party Gordon Brown said on Monday. A windfall tax would be imposed &quot;to create job opportunites and therefore reduce social security bills,&quot; Brown told BBC radio. He added that the minimum wage was part of Labour's employment policy, in order to help the low paid.</p>
</text>
